Codex work order (copy/paste)
1) Goals

Build a custom 404.html that:

Shows a full-bleed cinematic triptych background image (1920×1080).

Provides 4 interactive “portals”:

Left panel: Eli → /eli/

Middle panel: St33v™ → /st33vTM/

Right panel: Dr Morbius → /drMorbius/

A smaller “egg / note” hotspot (or button) → /sotd/

Provides a plain “Back to Home” link → /

Works on mobile and desktop.

Keyboard accessible (tab to each portal, visible focus ring).

Respects prefers-reduced-motion.

2) HTML structure

body full viewport, background image via <div class="bg">.

A <main class="overlay"> with:

A small title: 404

A one-liner: “This path doesn’t exist, but the universe does.”

Buttons row: Home + SOTD (text buttons)

Three big invisible <a class="zone zone-eli">, .zone-st33v, .zone-morbius positioned over the left/middle/right third of the image.

One smaller <a class="zone zone-sotd"> positioned over the “egg” area (middle panel, upper-right-ish), plus a label tooltip on hover/focus.

3) CSS behavior

Use background-image: url('/assets/404-triptych-wall.png'); (absolute path).

Add subtle hover/focus:

outline glow + mild zoom (transform: scale(1.01)) on the hovered zone via a pseudo-element.

Tooltip label appears on hover/focus (pure CSS).

Ensure readability of overlay text with a bottom gradient scrim.

4) Minimal JS (optional)

Not required. If used, only for:

Dynamically set the “requested path” text (optional), pulled from location.pathname and escaped.

Otherwise skip JS.

5) README instructions

Include:

Where to put 404.html, css/js, and assets/ in the deployed site root.

Nginx snippet:

error_page 404 /404.html;

location = /404.html {
    # internal;   # enable if you want it only as an error handler
}


Dotfile denial:

location ~ /\.(env|git|ht) {
